from ./Components import Components
from ./Compositions import Compositions
from ./Config import Config

export anchor Modules:
    description:
        Emul files and modules follow the same import and export behaviour as
        Piton. A design can be split across any number of files, and each file
        decides what the others may use.

    files:
        Emul source files carry the `.emul` extension. A directory with an
        `index.emul` file becomes a module.

    exporting:
        Putting `export` before a declaration makes it available to other
        files and modules. Both components and compositions can be exported.
        Anything that is not exported can only be used in its own file.

        ```emul
        \\\
        export component Button:
            padding: 8px 12px
        \\\
        ```

    importing:
        A file brings in exported declarations with `from`, a path, `import`,
        and a comma-separated list of names.

        ```emul
        \\\
        from ./Buttons import Button, IconButton
        \\\
        ```

        Importing a name that the other file does not export is a compiler
        error.

    paths:
        Import paths are relative to the current file. The `.emul` extension
        is optional, and the formatter removes it. A path of just `.` or `..`
        points at the `index.emul` in that directory.

        A path starting with `/` is absolute, measured from the project's
        source root, as set in @{Config}.

    aliasing:
        A name can be imported under a different name by writing the alias
        after it, with no keyword in between. The declaration is then
        available as, and only as, the alias.

        ```emul
        \\\
        from ./Buttons import Button PrimaryButton, IconButton
        \\\
        ```

    lineBreaks:
        An import may be split across lines, with `from`, the path and
        `import` on the first line and each name indented on its own line
        below. The formatter splits an import this way when it has more than
        two names or runs past 80 columns. It also sorts imports by path, and
        sorts the names within each one.

    modules:
        An `index.emul` gathers declarations from the files in its directory
        and exports them, so other files can import from the directory as a
        whole. It can do this in any of these ways:

        ```emul
        \\\
        // Import, then export
        from ./Button import Button
        export Button

        // Export directly from another file
        from ./Card export Card

        // Export everything another file exports
        from ./Forms export *

        // Export under a different name
        from ./Badge export Badge Tag
        \\\
        ```

    circularImports:
        Circular imports are supported and are not an error. Two files may
        import from each other. The only cycles that are errors are a component
        extending itself, directly or through other components, as described
        in @{Components}, and a composition containing itself, as described
        in @{Compositions}.

    rendering:
        Every composition exported from the entry file is rendered. The entry
        file is set in @{Config}. A
        composition that is not exported, or only exported from some other
        file, is not rendered on its own, though it can still be instanced in
        another composition, as described in @{Compositions}.
